# Pathland Java DSL — Current `.frame(...)` / `FrameMod` API & Opcode Emission

## 1. The current frame modifier type

### `FrameMod` (the only frame type)
**File:** `/Users/michael/Development/michaelkrog/Pathland/lib/java/pathland-view/src/main/java/com/pathland/view/FrameMod.java`

It is a `ViewModifier` (not a `View`), holding four nullable fields, and produces property mods via `Modified.props(...)`:

```java
6:  public final class FrameMod implements ViewModifier {
7:
8:      private final Float width;
9:      private final Float height;
10:     private final Float alignment;
11:     private final float[] bounds;
12:
13:     private FrameMod(Float width, Float height, Float alignment, float[] bounds) {
```

**All public factory overloads** (there is no public constructor):

| Lines | Signature | Emits |
|---|---|---|
| 30–32 | `of(float width)` | `WIDTH` only (no `HEIGHT`, no `ALIGNMENT`) |
| 39–41 | `of(float width, float height)` | `WIDTH` + `HEIGHT` |
| 47–49 | `of(float width, float height, Alignment alignment)` | `WIDTH` + `HEIGHT` + `ALIGNMENT` |
| 57–59 | `of(float width, Alignment alignment)` | `WIDTH` + `ALIGNMENT` |
| 68–72 | `of(minWidth, idealWidth, maxWidth, minHeight, idealHeight, maxHeight)` | `MIN_WIDTH`/`IDEAL_WIDTH`/`MAX_WIDTH`/`MIN_HEIGHT`/`IDEAL_HEIGHT`/`MAX_HEIGHT` (NaN/infinite omitted) |

**Emission body** (`FrameMod.java:74–111`):
```java
74:     public View body(View content) {
75:         if (bounds != null) {
...
78:             addBound(props, Properties.MIN_WIDTH, bounds[0]);
79:             addBound(props, Properties.IDEAL_WIDTH, bounds[1]);
80:             addBound(props, Properties.MAX_WIDTH, bounds[2]);
81:             addBound(props, Properties.MIN_HEIGHT, bounds[3]);
82:             addBound(props, Properties.IDEAL_HEIGHT, bounds[4]);
83:             addBound(props, Properties.MAX_HEIGHT, bounds[5]);
...
87:         if (width != null) {
88:             props.add(Modified.prop(Properties.WIDTH, fillOr(width)));
89:         }
90:         if (height != null) {
91:             props.add(Modified.prop(Properties.HEIGHT, fillOr(height)));
92:         }
93:         if (alignment != null) {
94:             props.add(Modified.prop(Properties.ALIGNMENT, alignment));
95:         }
...
99:     private static void addBound(...) {
100:        if (!Float.isNaN(value) && !Float.isInfinite(value)) { props.add(...); }
...
109:    private static float fillOr(float value) {
110:        return Float.isInfinite(value) ? Commands.Size.FILL : value;
111:    }
```

Key facts:
- `alignment` is stored as a `float` — the `Alignment.wire()` enum code (`FrameMod.java:48,58`).
- Infinite width/height (both `+∞` and `−∞`, `Float.isInfinite`) is normalized to `Commands.Size.FILL` (−1); finite values pass through. **`HUG_CONTENT` (−2) is never produced by `FrameMod`** — only `FILL` is.
- The min/ideal/max overload is mutually exclusive with the width/height overload (it sets `bounds != null`).
- **No reactive `Signal` overloads exist** for frame (contrast: `ForegroundStyle.of(Signal)`, `Background.of(Signal)`, `FontSize.of(Signal)` do exist). Frame is static-only today.

### How views chain it: `.with(...)` only — there is NO `.frame(...)`
- `View.with(ViewModifier...)` is the sole mechanism: `/Users/michael/Development/michaelkrog/Pathland/lib/java/pathland-view/src/main/java/com/pathland/view/View.java:58–64`
```java
58:     default View with(ViewModifier... modifiers) {
59:         View result = this;
60:         for (ViewModifier modifier : modifiers) {
61:             result = Modified.apply(result, modifier);
62:         }
63:         return result;
64:     }
```
- `View` has a few sugar defaults (`font` L71, `navigate`/`push`/`replace` L81–93, `environment` L102–113, `onPathChange` L120) but **no `frame(...)` default, and there is no `Modifiers` helper class** (no `Modifiers.java` in the tree).
- Confirmed by repo-wide search `.frame(`: the only Java hits are `sink.frame()` (the wire `Frame`, not sizing) and documentation. The Rust DSL *does* have `.frame(width, height, alignment)` at `/Users/michael/Development/michaelkrog/Pathland/lib/rust/crates/pathland-view/src/lib.rs:261–279` (for parity context).

### Every frame/size/width/height-related file in `.../com/pathland/view/`
| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `FrameMod.java` | The frame modifier (sizing) |
| `FixedSize.java` | `FIXED_SIZE_HORIZONTAL`/`VERTICAL` (intrinsic size) |
| `LayoutPriority.java` | `LAYOUT_PRIORITY` |
| `AspectRatio.java` | `ASPECT_RATIO` + `CONTENT_MODE` |
| `ScaledToFit.java` / `ScaledToFill.java` | `CONTENT_MODE` = Fit/Fill |
| `MinimumScaleFactor.java` | `MINIMUM_SCALE_FACTOR` |
| `SizeThatFits.java` + `Fit.java` | `SIZE_THAT_FITS` fit-slot (FIT_QUERY), *not* frame |
| `ContentMode.java` | Fit=0/Fill=1 enum |
| `Alignment.java` (2D, 9 values), `HorizontalAlignment.java`, `VerticalAlignment.java` | Alignment enums |
| `emit/Frame.java`, `emit/FrameOpcodeSink.java`, `transport/FrameCodec.java` | Wire **frame** (batch of opcodes) — unrelated to sizing |

There is **no** `Frame.java` sizing type, `FlexibleFrameProvider`, `Resizable`, or `ScaledToFit`-style frame provider (the `ScaledTo*` classes above are content-mode modifiers).

---

## 2. Where the emitter emits WIDTH / HEIGHT / size

**File:** `/Users/michael/Development/michaelkrog/Pathland/lib/java/pathland-view/src/main/java/com/pathland/view/emit/Emitter.java`

`FrameMod.body(...)` builds `Modified.props(content, Prop...)`; `Modified.render` stores each prop into `node.properties` (`Modified.java:64–73`). The emitter then walks the tree:

```java
238:    private void emitNode(PathlandNode node) {
239:        sink.createNode(node.id, node.component);
...
256:        for (Map.Entry<Integer, Object> entry : node.properties.entrySet()) {
257:            emitProperty(node.id, entry.getKey(), entry.getValue());
258:        }
...
269:    private void emitProperty(int nodeId, int property, Object value) {
270:        int valueType = value instanceof Color c && c.isToken()
271:                ? ValueTypes.DESIGN_TOKEN
272:                : ValueTypes.forProperty(property);
273:        sink.setProperty(nodeId, property, valueType, value);
274:    }
```

Value-type resolution — `ValueTypes.forProperty` (`ValueTypes.java:18–41`): `WIDTH`/`HEIGHT` and `MIN_/IDEAL_/MAX_*` are not listed, so they hit `default -> F32` (line 39). `ALIGNMENT` is explicitly `F32` (lines 35–38, comment: "Enums ride the wire as F32 holding the numeric enum code").

Wire encoding — `FrameOpcodeSink.setProperty` (`FrameOpcodeSink.java:84–111`):
```java
84:     public void setProperty(int nodeId, int property, int valueType, Object value) {
85:         int b = (valueType << 16) | (property & 0xFFFF);
...
108:        } else {
109:            push(Categories.PARAMETER, Commands.Parameter.SET_PROPERTY, 0, nodeId, b, ValueEncoder.encodeBits(valueType, value));
110:        }
```

`ValueEncoder.encodeBits` (`ValueEncoder.java:12–19`): `F32 -> Float.floatToRawIntBits((Float) value)`, placed in **C**.

So a fixed box becomes, per axis, one `PARAMETER::SET_PROPERTY`:
- `A = nodeId`, `B = (0x04 << 16) | 0x100B` (F32, WIDTH) / `(0x04 << 16) | 0x100C` (HEIGHT), `C = float bits of the value` — with `FILL = -1.0f` when `±∞` was passed to `FrameMod`.
- `ALIGNMENT` becomes `B = (0x04 << 16) | 0x0002`, `C = float bits of the 0–8 enum code`.
- All six bounds become separate `SET_PROPERTY` opcodes with `F32`; unset/NaN/infinite bounds are omitted by `addBound`.

Diffing on reconcile: `Emitter.reconcileNode` (`Emitter.java:502–508`) only emits a property when `!propertyValuesEqual(...)`.

`FILL`/`HUG` sentinels are defined in `Commands.Size` (`Commands.java:106–111`):
```java
107:    public static final class Size {
108:        public static final float FILL = -1f;
109:        public static final float HUG_CONTENT = -2f;
```
`FrameMod` normalizes only `FILL`; `HUG_CONTENT` is not currently produced by any Java frame path (it's a protocol-level sentinel).

---

## 3. Property-id constants in the Java DSL

**File:** `/Users/michael/Development/michaelkrog/Pathland/lib/java/pathland-view/src/main/java/com/pathland/view/Properties.java` (javadoc line 3: "mirrors `pathland_core::property_id`"). All frame-related IDs **do exist**:

